==Battleground==
*10 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 5 seconds<sup>150f</sup>, delay 10~15 seconds<sup>300f~450f</sup>.
*10 [[Gabriel]]s (500%) spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Gabriel]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
**4 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**3 [[Li'l Zyclone]]s spawn, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
**2 [[Angelic Gory|Angelic Gories]] spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**2 [[St. Dober]]s spawn, delay 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main issue of this stage is the Li'l Zyclone burrowing behind your units and stopping your meatshields. [[:Category:Cats with Knockback ability|Units with Knockback]] like [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Ectoweight]] are effective at stopping the Li'l Zyclone. From there just kill the Li'l Zyclones with things like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]] and then use attackers along with debuffers such as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo]], [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]], and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] to quickly deal with the St. Dober.


On higher crown difficulties, one can just Anti-Surge St. Dober to death with units like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] and Talented [[Li'l Lizard Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l King Dragon Cat]] while Ectoweight does his thing and [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] walls everything.

==Trivia==
*The word ''präparat'' in Microscope Bridge's Japanese name, Präparat Bridge, is a German word meaning "preparation" or a prepared specimen microscope slide.
*In the Italian Translation, the Name was Mistranslated to "Ponte Microscopico", or Microscopic Bridge.

